# Sensitive env file

`.env.local` is a secrets file. Do not read, search, list, print, or edit it unless the user explicitly asks you to open that file in the current request.

This includes Read, Grep, shell commands such as `Get-Content` or `Select-String`, and any rewrite of the file.

`example.env` is the template. Add new variable names there. Tell the user which names to copy into `.env.local`. Do not copy values out of `.env.local` to fill the example.
